.TH CTPOOL_CREATE 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_create \- create a thread pool with default memory management
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadpool.h>

ctpool ctpool_create(size_t num_threads,
                     size_t queue_capacity,
                     char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
A wrapper around ctpool_create_mp with mprocs = NULL, so the pool uses
the standard malloc and free for every allocation it makes.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
num_threads    Number of worker threads (must be >= 1)
queue_capacity 0 for unbounded; N > 0 for bounded. ccol_invalid_size
               is refused (see ctpool_create_mp(3)).
err_str        Optional. It gets a static error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns a new ctpool handle on success, or CTPOOL_INVALID on failure.
A process with no thread-specific key left to give gets CTPOOL_INVALID
from this call and from every later one; see ctpool_create_mp(3).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_create_mp (3),
.BR ctpool_construct (3)
